# 1️⃣ Build Heap

## 📖 What is Build Heap?

Given an unsorted array, we can convert it into a valid Heap.

Example:

```text
Input:

[4, 10, 3, 5, 1]
```

Build a Max Heap:

```text
        10
       /  \
      5    3
     / \
    4   1
```

Array representation:

```text
[10, 5, 3, 4, 1]
```

---

# 2️⃣ Important Observation

For a 0-indexed array:

```text
Parent = (i - 1) / 2
Left Child = 2*i + 1
Right Child = 2*i + 2
```

All leaf nodes are already valid heaps because they have no children.

Therefore, we only need to heapify the **non-leaf nodes**.

The last non-leaf node is:

```text
(n / 2) - 1
```

---

# 3️⃣ Bottom-Up Heap Construction

For a Max Heap:

```text
Start from:

(n / 2) - 1
```

and move toward:

```text
0
```

At every index:

```text
Heapify Down
```

---

# 4️⃣ Max Heapify

For every node:

```text
Parent >= Left Child
Parent >= Right Child
```

If this property is violated, swap the node with its larger child.

### C++ Code

```cpp
void maxHeapify(
    vector<int>& arr,
    int n,
    int i)
{
    int largest = i;

    int left = 2 * i + 1;
    int right = 2 * i + 2;

    if(left < n &&
       arr[left] > arr[largest])
    {
        largest = left;
    }

    if(right < n &&
       arr[right] > arr[largest])
    {
        largest = right;
    }

    if(largest != i)
    {
        swap(arr[i], arr[largest]);

        maxHeapify(
            arr,
            n,
            largest
        );
    }
}
```

---

# 5️⃣ Build Max Heap

### C++ Code

```cpp
void buildMaxHeap(vector<int>& arr)
{
    int n = arr.size();

    for(int i = n / 2 - 1;
        i >= 0;
        i--)
    {
        maxHeapify(arr, n, i);
    }
}
```

Example:

```text
Input:

[4, 10, 3, 5, 1]
```

After Build Max Heap:

```text
[10, 5, 3, 4, 1]
```

---

# 6️⃣ Min Heapify

For a Min Heap:

```text
Parent <= Left Child
Parent <= Right Child
```

We select the smallest child.

### C++ Code

```cpp
void minHeapify(
    vector<int>& arr,
    int n,
    int i)
{
    int smallest = i;

    int left = 2 * i + 1;
    int right = 2 * i + 2;

    if(left < n &&
       arr[left] < arr[smallest])
    {
        smallest = left;
    }

    if(right < n &&
       arr[right] < arr[smallest])
    {
        smallest = right;
    }

    if(smallest != i)
    {
        swap(arr[i], arr[smallest]);

        minHeapify(
            arr,
            n,
            smallest
        );
    }
}
```

---

# 7️⃣ Build Min Heap

### C++ Code

```cpp
void buildMinHeap(vector<int>& arr)
{
    int n = arr.size();

    for(int i = n / 2 - 1;
        i >= 0;
        i--)
    {
        minHeapify(arr, n, i);
    }
}
```

