# 9️⃣ Heap Sort

## 📖 What is Heap Sort?

Heap Sort is a comparison-based sorting algorithm that uses a Heap.

For ascending order:

```text
Build Max Heap
```

Then repeatedly:

```text
Move Maximum to End
Heapify Remaining Elements
```

---

# 🔟 Heap Sort Steps

Suppose:

```text
[4, 10, 3, 5, 1]
```

### Step 1

Build Max Heap:

```text
[10, 5, 3, 4, 1]
```

### Step 2

Swap root with last element:

```text
[1, 5, 3, 4, 10]
```

`10` is now in its correct position.

### Step 3

Heapify remaining elements:

```text
[5, 4, 3, 1, 10]
```

### Step 4

Repeat.

Final result:

```text
[1, 3, 4, 5, 10]
```

---

# 1️⃣1️⃣ Heap Sort Implementation

### C++ Code

```cpp
void maxHeapify(
    vector<int>& arr,
    int n,
    int i)
{
    int largest = i;

    int left = 2 * i + 1;
    int right = 2 * i + 2;

    if(left < n &&
       arr[left] > arr[largest])
    {
        largest = left;
    }

    if(right < n &&
       arr[right] > arr[largest])
    {
        largest = right;
    }

    if(largest != i)
    {
        swap(arr[i], arr[largest]);

        maxHeapify(
            arr,
            n,
            largest
        );
    }
}

void heapSort(vector<int>& arr)
{
    int n = arr.size();

    // Build Max Heap
    for(int i = n / 2 - 1;
        i >= 0;
        i--)
    {
        maxHeapify(arr, n, i);
    }

    // Extract elements
    for(int i = n - 1;
        i > 0;
        i--)
    {
        swap(arr[0], arr[i]);

        maxHeapify(arr, i, 0);
    }
}
```

---

# 1️⃣2️⃣ Heap Sort Complexity

```text
Build Heap → O(n)
```

Then:

```text
n Heapify operations
```

Each takes:

```text
O(log n)
```

Therefore:

```text
Time → O(n log n)
```

Space:

```text
O(1)
```

Heap Sort is an **in-place sorting algorithm**.

---

# 📊 Heap Sort Properties

| Property | Heap Sort |
|----------|-----------|
| Best Case | O(n log n) |
| Average Case | O(n log n) |
| Worst Case | O(n log n) |
| Extra Space | O(1) |
| Stable | No |
| In-place | Yes |

