# 1️⃣3️⃣ Kth Largest Element

## 📖 Problem

Find the kth largest element in an array.

Example:

```text
arr = [3, 2, 1, 5, 6, 4]

k = 2
```

Sorted:

```text
1 2 3 4 5 6
```

2nd largest:

```text
5
```

---

# 1️⃣4️⃣ Approach Using Min Heap

Maintain a Min Heap of size `k`.

For every element:

```text
Push element
```

If heap size becomes greater than `k`:

```text
Pop minimum
```

At the end:

```text
Heap Top = Kth Largest
```

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
int kthLargest(
    vector<int>& nums,
    int k)
{
    priority_queue<
        int,
        vector<int>,
        greater<int>
    > pq;

    for(int num : nums)
    {
        pq.push(num);

        if(pq.size() > k)
        {
            pq.pop();
        }
    }

    return pq.top();
}
```

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(n log k)

Space: O(k)
```

---

# 1️⃣5️⃣ Kth Smallest Element

For kth smallest, use a **Max Heap of size k**.

Why?

We want to keep the smallest `k` elements.

The largest among those `k` elements will be at the root.

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
int kthSmallest(
    vector<int>& nums,
    int k)
{
    priority_queue<int> pq;

    for(int num : nums)
    {
        pq.push(num);

        if(pq.size() > k)
        {
            pq.pop();
        }
    }

    return pq.top();
}
```

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(n log k)

Space: O(k)
```

---

# 1️⃣6️⃣ Kth Largest vs Kth Smallest

| Problem | Heap Used |
|---------|-----------|
| Kth Largest | Min Heap |
| Kth Smallest | Max Heap |

Remember:

```text
Kth Largest
→ Min Heap of size K
```

```text
Kth Smallest
→ Max Heap of size K
```

