# 1️⃣7️⃣ Top K Frequent Elements

## 📖 Problem

Find the `k` most frequent elements.

Example:

```text
nums = [1,1,1,2,2,3]

k = 2
```

Frequencies:

```text
1 → 3
2 → 2
3 → 1
```

Answer:

```text
[1, 2]
```

---

# 1️⃣8️⃣ Approach

Use:

```text
Hash Map + Min Heap
```

The map stores:

```text
element → frequency
```

Then maintain a Min Heap of size `k`.

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
vector<int> topKFrequent(
    vector<int>& nums,
    int k)
{
    unordered_map<int, int> freq;

    for(int num : nums)
    {
        freq[num]++;
    }

    priority_queue<
        pair<int, int>,
        vector<pair<int, int>>,
        greater<pair<int, int>>
    > pq;

    for(auto& [num, count] : freq)
    {
        pq.push({count, num});

        if(pq.size() > k)
        {
            pq.pop();
        }
    }

    vector<int> answer;

    while(!pq.empty())
    {
        answer.push_back(pq.top().second);
        pq.pop();
    }

    return answer;
}
```

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(n log k)

Space: O(n)
```

