# 1️⃣9️⃣ K Closest Elements / Points

Heaps are very useful when we need the:

```text
K closest
K smallest
K largest
```

elements.

For example:

```text
K closest points to origin
```

Distance:

```text
distance² = x² + y²
```

We can maintain a Max Heap of size `k`.

Why Max Heap?

Because we want to remove the farthest point whenever the heap contains more than `k` points.

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
vector<vector<int>> kClosest(
    vector<vector<int>>& points,
    int k)
{
    priority_queue<
        pair<int, pair<int, int>>
    > pq;

    for(auto& point : points)
    {
        int x = point[0];
        int y = point[1];

        int distance =
            x * x + y * y;

        pq.push({
            distance,
            {x, y}
        });

        if(pq.size() > k)
        {
            pq.pop();
        }
    }

    vector<vector<int>> answer;

    while(!pq.empty())
    {
        auto point = pq.top();

        pq.pop();

        answer.push_back({
            point.second.first,
            point.second.second
        });
    }

    return answer;
}
```

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(n log k)

Space: O(k)
```

