# 2️⃣0️⃣ Top-K Pattern

A very important interview pattern:

```text
Need K Largest
→ Min Heap of size K
```

```text
Need K Smallest
→ Max Heap of size K
```

```text
Need K Closest
→ Max Heap of size K
```

```text
Need K Farthest
→ Min Heap of size K
```

---

# 2️⃣1️⃣ Why Heap Size K?

Suppose:

```text
n = 1,000,000
```

and:

```text
k = 5
```

We don't need to store all million elements in the heap.

We only maintain:

```text
5 elements
```

Therefore:

```text
Space = O(k)
```

and operations become:

```text
O(log k)
```

instead of:

```text
O(log n)
```

---

