# 💡 Interview Tips

✅ Build Heap using bottom-up heapification in O(n).

✅ Heap Sort uses a Max Heap for ascending order.

✅ For Kth Largest, use a Min Heap of size K.

✅ For Kth Smallest, use a Max Heap of size K.

✅ For Top K problems, try to maintain a heap of size K.

✅ Use a Max Heap when you need to remove the largest candidate.

✅ Use a Min Heap when you need to remove the smallest candidate.

---

# ⚠️ Common Mistakes

❌ Assuming Build Heap takes O(n log n).

❌ Using the wrong heap for Kth Largest/Smallest.

❌ Maintaining a heap of size `n` when only `k` elements are needed.

❌ Forgetting that C++ `priority_queue` is a Max Heap by default.

❌ Confusing Heap Sort with a stable sorting algorithm.

❌ Forgetting to reduce the heap size during Heap Sort.

